<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00048</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>166d886e-fbf6-4a38-9e76-88e2a12bb14d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para class="os-raise-text-bold"><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></para>
<para>For questions 1–5, use the following scenario to identify the expression, equation, or inequality described.</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>To support a local senior citizens center, a student club sent a flier home to the \(𝑛\) students in the school. The flier said, “Please bring in money to support the senior citizens center. Paper money and coins accepted!” Their goal is to raise \(𝑇\) dollars.</para>
</blockquote>
<para>Choose the expression, equation, or inequality, from the
  list, that describes the given quantity.</para>
<list>
  <item>\(T+50\)</item>
  <item>\(0.5T\)</item>
  <item>\(0.25n\)</item>
  <item>\(0.5n\)</item>
  <item> \(T-0.5n\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> The dollar amount the club would have if they
    reached half of their goal. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0.5T\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> The dollar
    amount the club would have if every student at the school donated 50 cents to
    the cause. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0.5n\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> The dollar amount the club could donate if they
    made $50 more than their goal. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(T+50\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> The dollar amount the club would still need to
    raise to reach its goal after every student at the school donated 50 cents. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(T-.05n\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> The dollar amount the club would have if half of
    the students at the school each gave 50 cents. </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(0.25n\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> Each of the 10 students in the baking club made 2 chocolate cakes for a fundraiser. They all used the same recipe, using \(c\) cups of flour in total.</item>
</list>
<para>Write an expression that represents the amount of flour required for one cake.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>:</emphasis> \(\frac{c}{20}\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Determine if each is an expression or an equation: </item>
</list>
<para>\(3(x - 7) = 27\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>equation</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Determine if each is an expression or an equation: </item>
</list>
<para>\(5(4y - 2) - 7\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> expression</para>
<para>For questions 9-10, choose the
  algebraic expression that represents the English phrase</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>the
    difference of \(14x\) ² and 13 </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(14x^2-13\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>the quotient of \(12x\) and 2</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(\frac{12x}2\)</para>
</section>
